* text=auto eol=lf

*.blade.php diff=html
*.css diff=css
*.html diff=html
*.md diff=markdown
*.php diff=php

# Concurrent decision tickets both append to the tail of the log, so git sees
# two edits to one line and conflicts every time (UAMS-Web/uams-statamic-archive#2445). `union` resolves that
# by keeping both appends -- WHERE THE ATTRIBUTE IS ALREADY IN EFFECT on both
# sides of the merge. That is the ordinary case and it is why the line is here.
#
# It does NOT order the result -- it appends ours-then-theirs -- which is what
# `scripts/check-decision-log-order.mjs` is for, and why the driver alone is not
# sufficient. This half is unconditional and is the load-bearing one.
#
# SYNCING A BRANCH THAT PREDATES THIS LINE can still conflict, because an
# attribute arriving IN a merge does not govern that merge. A conflict there is
# NOT a missing or broken driver and not a defect in your tree: resolve it, and
# let the order guard gate the result. Whether the merge refuses is not a signal
# to build on -- the order guard is the gate. Measured on two platforms and
# four git binaries; the table is in `docs/DECISIONS.md` (UAMS-Web/uams-statamic-archive#2471).
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union

/.github export-ignore
CHANGELOG.md export-ignore
.styleci.yml export-ignore
